OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA largely dry start with sunny
OL,6,Fspells, but showers across Argyll and
OL,7,Fthe west develop more widely through
OL,8,Fthe morning. The showers become
OL,9,Foccasionally heavy in the afternoon,
OL,10,Fand wintry on higher mountains, as
OL,11,Fwinds turn more northwesterly and
OL,12,Ffreshen.
OL,13,
OL,14,CTonight:FShowers die out through the
OL,15,Fevening and winds ease. With long
OL,16,Fclear spells developing it will be a
OL,17,Fchilly night with a risk of frost in
OL,18,Fsheltered spots.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
